{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>If a soul sins unwittingly</b> — Because thought resides in the soul, and it is the soul that sins unwittingly, Scripture mentions \"soul\" here. The reason for offerings upon the unwitting soul is that all iniquities produce a blemish in the soul; they are a defect in it, and it will not merit to stand before its Maker unless it is purified from all sin. Were it not for this, the foolishness of the nations would gain them entry before Him. Therefore the unwitting soul brings an offering, that it may merit closeness to the Elohim who gave it, and for this reason as well Scripture mentions \"soul.\" And our Sages expounded (Sifra ad loc.): \"soul\" — to include converts and slaves. Now, in the case of the sin of the anointed priest, Scripture did not mention \"and he shall make atonement for him and he shall be forgiven,\" as it mentioned for the other sinners — the congregation, the ruler, and the commoner — perhaps because of his great eminence he is not fully atoned and forgiven until he prays and supplicates his Elohim, for he is the angel of YHWH of Hosts and must be blameless and pure of hands. And here, regarding the bulls burned with the incensing of the emurim, Scripture did not mention \"a sweet savour\" nor \"an offering made by fire to YHWH,\" the reason being that since part of them is offered outside, they are not an offering made by fire to YHWH. And in the case of the ruler's goat it mentioned atonement but did not mention \"an offering made by fire, a sweet savour to YHWH\" (Numbers 28:8), because the offering is a goat. And in the case of the individual's sin-offering it mentioned \"for a sweet savour to YHWH\" but did not mention \"an offering made by fire,\" since it is understood that it is an offering made by fire, for the entire intent is an offering made by fire to YHWH. And the enlightened will understand:"], :book :leviticus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {0 "The citation Numbers 28:8 appears to refer to the ruler's sin-offering passage; the verse reference is as given in the Hebrew, though it does not correspond to the standard content of Numbers 28:8."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:50:10.373653340Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}